  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason (skewness, i.e., concentration of probability on favorable outcomes) overlaps with the individual's focus on the high probability of winning something in Lottery B versus the higher chance of nothing in Lottery A. Although the term 'skewness' is not used, the individual is effectively responding to the more left-skewed nature of Lottery B—assigning greater weight to its high probability of a favorable (non-zero) outcome. The justification aligns with the rule of the decision reason: preferring the lottery with more probability mass on favorable results. While the reasoning is not framed in technical terms, the cognitive process described mirrors the essence of the skewness-based rule. Therefore, it is highly likely the individual used a form of reasoning consistent with the given decision reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 90
